Z||000000||johnt671||07-08-2001||02:13 PM||||Every time I blow the horn the warning chime goes off.  Any ideas what to check?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Dave Gunsul||07-08-2001||04:46 PM||||Oh, I thought you ment that you got really<BR>excited when you blew the horn.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>As in; you got a boinger when you blow the horn.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||10
Z||000002||hugh||07-08-2001||06:36 PM||||As I've said in the past,I'm not real familiar with these cars even though I have 2 of them.When you get something happening  that doesn't make a lot of sense start checking grounds.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/hugh_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Songman||07-08-2001||07:48 PM||||They go off for lots of reasons. The one in my white 88 used to go off every time I hit a bump. Check out Ogre's Cave about this, or if you can stand it and remember to turn off your lights and remove your keys and take the parking brake off, just reach up underthe dash on the passenger side and remove the blue box.<P>You can see where mine is now in the picture below. It has been in the dash pocket for close to 6 months now!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mycars4.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||07-08-2001||09:07 PM||||You <I>must</I> get your PFF technical terms correct.  The correct name is "blue dingy thingy".  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  You're new.  You're forgiven.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000005||Ken Wittlief||07-09-2001||09:13 AM||||the alarm goes off when you blow your horn when its not really necessary - its a feature!<P>or maybe you have one of the senior citizen models - the alarm goes off to let you know you are blowing your horn. (c%||||reg||11
Z||000006||Galen||07-09-2001||09:43 AM||||MM, I Personally feel that boinger is kinda an exotic word..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> but on to what I really am saying.. what Songman said  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> hehe.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/redcreature.gif">   <BR><FONT SIZE="1">To whom it may concern, The preceeding message was the opinion of this person and not of this forum. If you do not like it. Oh well</FONT>||||reg||1
